	doi = {10.1139/f94-013},
	abstract = {Relationships between various biological reference points (BRPs) used to define thresholds and targets of fisheries management strategies were examined for a range of combinations of life history characteristics. Rank orderings of the selected BRPs were strongly influenced by the degree of density dependence in the underlying spawning–recruitment (S–R) relationship. The validity of F
