	abstract = {The maximum sustainable yield (MSY) concept is widely considered to be outdated and misleading. In response, ﬁsheries scientists have developed models that often diverge radically from the ﬁrst operational version of the concept. We show that the original MSY concept was deeply rooted in ecology and that going back to that version would be beneﬁcial for ﬁsheries, not least because the various substitutes have not served us well.},
